        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                "word": "lexème",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2e3552f3-ac34-46ce-89b3-59b12e5397d4",
                        "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lexèmes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d41d8aa2-2abd-38b6-822e-a78bd783a40a",
                        "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unité minimale de sens et de forme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc93198d-b9bb-4317-ad56-4a5ada9518af",
                                "sense_id": "d41d8aa2-2abd-38b6-822e-a78bd783a40a",
                                "text": "L’origine onomatopéique d’un lexème est une question diachronique, sans pertinence en tant que telle pour la sémantique de la parole : ainsi, il n’est pas fondamental pour nous de trancher parmi les nombreux cas qui peuvent faire débats (quid de gong, flaque, grogner, grommeler, siffler, claquer, vrombir… ?)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "297c4209-8b4e-4ee9-bac3-4961b95de987",
                                "sense_id": "d41d8aa2-2abd-38b6-822e-a78bd783a40a",
                                "text": "Un lexème verbal est constitué d’un squelette consonantique, d’un schème tonal et d’un support vocalique neutre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ada5741-13e0-3d96-aac1-0f31e7659cdb",
                        "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Morphème lexical, qui appartient à une liste non finie des mots de la langue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb3f0e74-4f5d-40fc-9187-e6530d468054",
                                "sense_id": "1ada5741-13e0-3d96-aac1-0f31e7659cdb",
                                "text": "Au plan morphologique, il existe un continuum entre lexèmes et grammèmes, lié au processus de grammaticalisation."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "077fad3b-b0ea-370a-84bf-ace71daf83bd",
                        "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Représentation abstraite d’un mot englobant l’ensemble de ses réalisations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39155b6b-4a90-4216-8c2a-6e6708196fc2",
                                "sense_id": "077fad3b-b0ea-370a-84bf-ace71daf83bd",
                                "text": "Une description constructive ne fait de prédictions directes que sur les formes des lexèmes qu’elle connaît : étant donné que les lexèmes sont typiquement organisés en classes flexionnelles et que les règles de réalisation sont typiquement dépendantes de ces classes, il n’y a pas de réponse à la question de savoir quelle forme doit être générée pour un lexème nouveau."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4fff833-2882-3dde-be0c-e66175e5ffcc",
                        "entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Occurrence unique d’une suite continue de caractères."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Analyse lexicale"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87fb96de-b709-4120-ad9d-6b18c48ebe4d",
                                "sense_id": "c4fff833-2882-3dde-be0c-e66175e5ffcc",
                                "text": "Pour le moment, nous pensons que les applications les plus prometteuses et réalistes du TAL concernent l’évaluation de productions lexicales simples (lexèmes, expressions semi figées, expressions idiomatiques, etc.)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb36b249-10db-4fd9-a6e1-14ad4817e97b",
                        "source_entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lexem",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lexem",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e29cd73e-fe86-34ce-8568-2530c527d3ea",
                                        "entry_id": "6e8a6941-9c49-3aef-a33f-898dfa01b846",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grundform, Stichwort im Lexikon; Einheit der (Langue)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0528bb8-e224-464a-b5ed-f07499201cf5",
                                                "sense_id": "e29cd73e-fe86-34ce-8568-2530c527d3ea",
                                                "text": "\"Wort\" als Stichwort im Lexikon ist ein Lexem, das für die Wortformen \"Wort\", \"Wortes\", \"Worte\", \"Wörter\" und \"Wörtern\" steht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec376698-b7fb-4e5f-97f3-142fcdd32cb4",
                                                "sense_id": "e29cd73e-fe86-34ce-8568-2530c527d3ea",
                                                "text": "„Kohyponyme sind Lexeme, die sich gleichrangig auf das gleiche Hyperonym beziehen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82459c5a-fa61-48a9-92cc-7d8a788f9064",
                                                "sense_id": "e29cd73e-fe86-34ce-8568-2530c527d3ea",
                                                "text": "„Sowohl 1940 als auch 1999 sind einige Lexeme nicht anzutreffen, die heute allgemein bekannt sind, oft sogar als Modewörter bezeichnet werden.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "280c5951-2925-322f-bdc2-c87fdb5f608a",
                                        "entry_id": "6e8a6941-9c49-3aef-a33f-898dfa01b846",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "freies oder gebundenes Morphem mit lexikalischer Bedeutung"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e843f657-2947-496e-8c2a-86a1af533282",
                                                "sense_id": "280c5951-2925-322f-bdc2-c87fdb5f608a",
                                                "text": "\"schreib-\" ist ein gebundenes lexikalisches Morphem; \"Tisch\" ist ein freies lexikalisches Morphem; beide sind Lexeme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4437b9a-83ce-455f-808b-b3d0875fa8e2",
                                                "sense_id": "280c5951-2925-322f-bdc2-c87fdb5f608a",
                                                "text": "„Pronominaladverbien sind feste Lexeme und können nach der geltenden Norm nicht in ihre Bestandteile zerlegt werden, also Satzklammern bilden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f432526-5282-458f-be88-e9edc72bc99d",
                                                "sense_id": "280c5951-2925-322f-bdc2-c87fdb5f608a",
                                                "text": "„Der jährliche Zugang an neuen Fachwörtern ist mit circa 250000 Lexemen sicher nicht zu hoch geschätzt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f84ef1ce-702b-4e87-8a91-a9646a0db02d",
                                                "sense_id": "280c5951-2925-322f-bdc2-c87fdb5f608a",
                                                "text": "„Durch Assoziation ruft das eine Lexem gleichsam die anderen herbei und tastet ihre Bedeutungen auf hilfreiche Merkmale ab.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c85a7ac5-8d67-42a6-817a-8c7ea992b3cd",
                        "source_entry_id": "cbf46008-1d75-3476-a987-ba90edb4f983",
                        "target_lang_word": "lexeme",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lexeme",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d25e970c-3681-3b88-801f-81408bf345c0",
                                        "entry_id": "f627544e-f365-3f43-94fd-797645af6b19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lexical item corresponding to the set of all words (or of all multi-word expressions) that are semantically related through inflection of a particular shared basic form.",
                                            "The abstract minimum unit of language or meaning that underlies such a set."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd599434-48b0-4b6b-9074-4cf6177978f8",
                                                "sense_id": "d25e970c-3681-3b88-801f-81408bf345c0",
                                                "text": "A lexeme is a unit of lexical meaning, which exists regardless of any inflectional endings it may have or the number of words it may contain. Thus, fibrillate, rain cats and dogs, and come in are all lexemes, as are elephant, jog, cholesterol, happiness, put up with, face the music, and hundreds of thousands of other meaningful items in English."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a554163-39e4-4e20-98a6-c35997e38caa",
                                                "sense_id": "d25e970c-3681-3b88-801f-81408bf345c0",
                                                "text": "In a typical lexicalist approach (e.g. Koontz-Garboden 2006), the unmarked lexeme is taken as lexically listed, even if its meaning (as it often does) includes templatic entailments, and the derivational morphology is taken to operate on the underived form to yield the derived form. This is the case not only morphologically, but also semantically."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d84551a-73d1-37e5-b615-669d2e4e218e",
                                        "entry_id": "f627544e-f365-3f43-94fd-797645af6b19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lexical item corresponding to the set of all words (or of all multi-word expressions) that are semantically related through inflection of a particular shared basic form.",
                                            "The set itself; a lexemic family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67b7694e-fa54-3f8f-be01-9840ebcd4431",
                                        "entry_id": "f627544e-f365-3f43-94fd-797645af6b19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lexical item corresponding to the set of all words (or of all multi-word expressions) that are semantically related through inflection of a particular shared basic form.",
                                            "The wordform chosen to represent such a set or family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45518490-129e-4399-a713-3dc8d3637232",
                                                "sense_id": "67b7694e-fa54-3f8f-be01-9840ebcd4431",
                                                "text": "For the second sense, where “word” means “item that should have its own dictionary entry,” lexicographers sometimes use the term “lemma,” but that has other meanings too, so among linguists the term lexeme is now standard, and I’ll use it. For the different forms or shapes that belong to a lexeme we can use the term word-form. ¶ And as a typographical convention, from now on I’ll always put lexeme names in bold italics with a capital letter. So I’ll say there is a lexeme called Pamper [emphasis in original]. It’s the name of a small collection of word-forms with particular spellings – four of them: pamper, pampered, pampering, and pampers. I will always put word-forms (and all the phrases and clauses I mention as examples) in italics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0444493-b571-3014-8b8d-d747e0c9e544",
                                        "entry_id": "f627544e-f365-3f43-94fd-797645af6b19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual instance of a continuous character sequence without spaces, used in lexical analysis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "039f499c-c407-446b-9347-333c6be7ffc1",
                                                "sense_id": "d0444493-b571-3014-8b8d-d747e0c9e544",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: token"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
